  "background_and_question": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Baltimore's Mayor and City Council",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ce7415c692bf858a28d41a6aca8c170a317841cb77e635290a80a9bfa08c7b81",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ce7415c692bf-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 2,
              "start": 2
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The City of Baltimore sued various energy companies in Maryland state court alleging concealment of environmental impacts of the fossil fuels they promoted."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "District Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ce7415c692bf858a28d41a6aca8c170a317841cb77e635290a80a9bfa08c7b81",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ce7415c692bf-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 2,
              "start": 2
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The district court agreed with the City and issued an order remanding the case back to state court."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ae28ba47a085c0207cea307a3d6e8fca5a69880230e8af03719b883d7a59e5ea",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ae28ba47a085-0002-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 45,
              "start": 45
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The case was not removed pursuant to \u00a7\u202f1442 because the petitioners did not qualify for federal\u2011officer removal."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ce7415c692bf858a28d41a6aca8c170a317841cb77e635290a80a9bfa08c7b81",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ce7415c692bf-0000-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 6,
              "start": 6
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Gorsuch, the central legal question is whether \u00a7\u202f1447(d) permits a court of appeals to review any issue in a district\u2011court remand order when the defendant premised removal, in part, on the federal\u2011officer removal statute (\u00a7\u202f1442) or the civil\u2011rights removal statute (\u00a7\u202f1443)."
      }
    ],
